    "faq": {
      "type": "etl-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "q1": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Can I negotiate an international teaching contract?",
            "answer": "<p>Often, yes. Schools expect a few questions. Start date, family flights, housing size and your placement on the salary scale are the terms most often adjusted. Ask once, in writing, and explain why.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q2": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How long is a typical international teaching contract?",
            "answer": "<p>Many international schools offer an initial contract of two years, sometimes renewable year by year after that. Check the length, the notice period and the renewal terms in your own contract.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q3": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What is end-of-service gratuity?",
            "answer": "<p>A payment many Gulf employers must make when your contract ends, usually based on your basic salary and years of service. In the UAE it is 21 days' basic salary per year for the first five years; in Qatar the legal minimum is three weeks' basic salary per year.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q4": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is it normal for a school to keep my passport?",
            "answer": "<p>No. A school may hold it briefly to process your visa, but it should be returned straight away. UAE law says employers must not withhold workers' official documents, and Qatar fines employers who confiscate passports.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q5": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Should I pay a fee to get a teaching job abroad?",
            "answer": "<p>Be careful. International fair-recruitment principles say workers should not pay recruitment fees. A registration fee for a recruitment service or job fair is different from paying for a specific offer, so check what the fee covers.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q6": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What if the school promised something that isn't in the contract?",
            "answer": "<p>Ask for it to be added before you sign. The signed contract is what counts if there is a disagreement later.</p>"
          }
        },
        "q7": {
          "type": "qa",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What happens if I need to leave the contract early?",
            "answer": "<p>It depends on your contract and the country's labour law. Check the notice period and any repayment clause for flights, recruitment or visa costs before you sign, so you know the cost in advance.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
